So I started a lawful caveman on NAO following a wizard ascension. I am not 
used to play a caveman and It was an interesting game; I lost my pet on 
level 2 but managed to find some good armor in a used armor shop. On level 4 
I found a general store and lo and behold, a mjollnir was randomly generated 
on the floor. The storekeeper wanted 24,000zm for the weapon, but I was 
resolved to steal it.

I wandered down to level 5, where a bones file was in a scroll store. Maybe 
I can ID a teleport scroll, but no such luck. Down one more level was a 
another store, but nothing there either. Wandering if maybe one of the wands 
I had found was a wand of digging, I zapped it. Nothing. So it wasn't 
digging. But when I zapped it at a statue to test whether or not the statue 
would break (or change, or whatever) the statue disappeared. Aha! A further 
test proved it to be a wand of teleport.

Back up to level 4. I grabbed the hammer, a chain mail, some scrolls and 
other goodies, and teleported out. I made it to the down stairs for the 
mines before seeing either the cops or the angry storekeeper. Sweet success! 
The plan: advance skill in hammer and accumulate enough items/power that I 
could challenge the shopkeeper if needed when I got back. Such a stroke of 
luck is almost unprecedented in Nethack.

Two levels down a magic lamp was randomly generated (I price IDd it in 
minetown) and a magic marker was found in the hardware store in town. I 
enchanted mojo to +2 and worked up to skilled.

I reached mine's end, but had no means of liberating the luckstone (it was 
the level with the gnome king's wine cellar). Hoping that someone, somewhere 
had dropped a digging implement, I went back and looked around.

Next thing I know, my HP are at 0. DYWYPI. My caveman had fallen on poison 
spikes and died instantly. Sometimes you just have to wonder if the RNG is 
really evil or not. 




